hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"375","Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what is disliked among sacrificial animals and camels. He said: ""The one-eyed, the emaciated, and the one whose udders are all dried up."
"376","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Yahya, that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to him, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar, that it reached them that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sacrificial meat (may be kept) until the crescent of Muharram, for whoever wishes to delay that."
"377","Musaddad narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from al-Salt, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The slaughter of a Muslim is lawful, whether he mentioned the name of Allah or not; if he mentioned, he mentioned none but the name of Allah."
